add("beyondthebump-1wpvngj", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "tried_failed", ["night_wakings", "sleepwear", "price_value"], "Footie pajama and 0.5 sleep sack - too cold by the morning", "Room drops from 72 to 65 overnight; parent lists sleepwear combinations tried for a 5-month-old's wake-ups.")
add("beyondthebump-1wpvngj", "pbz64yl", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "price_signal", ["sleepwear", "price_value"], "I thought about that too I’m like all the ones I’ve bought already would equal a woolino and then some 🙄", "Weighing a premium wool sleep sack after buying several cheaper ones that did not solve the temperature problem.")
add("beyondthebump-1wpvngj", "peml34k", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "purchase", ["sleepwear", "price_value"], "OK, I need to update everybody. Woolino really is that girl I’m so happy we bought them.", "Two weeks later the parent reports back after buying the premium wool sleep sacks.")
add("sleeptrain-1wqe5ox", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "regret", ["course_purchase", "regression_4_month", "sleep_training_values"], "the program worked great for our first - the only problem we faced was kicking ourselves for waiting until 17 months. Definitely not doing that this time.", "Second baby in the 4-month regression; parents used a paid sleep course with their first child and want to start earlier.")
add("beyondthebump-1wrasjs", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "tried_failed", ["sleep_consultant", "price_value", "comparison_other_babies"], "We have seen a sleep consultant, paid for baby massage, bought everything you can buy, talked to the pediatrician, etc…", "Parent of a hard first year lists everything paid for; sleep still an issue at twelve months.")
add("beyondthebump-1wrasjs", "pcb2t4u", "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "others_said", ["comparison_other_babies", "guilt"], "my mother in law (who is so kind and not malicious) has made a lot of subtle comments agreeing that she is a really difficult baby compared to the other ones", "Relatives compare the baby with six cousins; parent worries something is wrong.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrcsar", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "question", ["course_purchase", "room_sharing", "personalization"], "We are thinking of trying Taking Cara Babies, but I know it recommends the baby is in his/her own room.", "Parents want to keep the baby in their room; unsure whether a course's own-room rule fits them.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrqgst", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["sleep_consultant", "chair_method", "pacifier"], "we decided to contact a sleep consultant and sleep train our 7mo boy. We went going cold turkey with the pacifier and did the sleep training (14-day Chair Method), and our boy successfully learnt to self-soothe and sleep on his own.", "Consultant-led chair method at 7 months worked; the post is about sleep falling apart again at 9 months.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrqgst", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "pain", ["wake_windows", "schedule_rigidity", "app_tracking"], "I am anxious 24/7, I am calculating every wake window by minute, and if we are late for 10-20 minutes, I lose my mind and expect the worst to happen.", "After a successful consultant plan, the mother is consumed by timing wake windows as naps fall apart.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrqgst", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "others_said", ["sleep_consultant", "schedule_rigidity"], "Our sleep consultant told me that baby’s sleep is “top priority” and I guess it all went too far.", "Mother links her anxiety to the consultant's framing of sleep.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrqgst", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "desire", ["wake_windows", "information_overload"], "Is this another regression? Is he overtired again? Is the schedule wrong again? I just want to relax and enjoy everything!", "Mother, mostly alone with the baby while husband works double shifts, asks strangers which of the usual explanations applies.")
add("sleeptrain-1ws3m1u", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["course_purchase", "night_wakings", "ferber"], "One night she was awake and on off cried for 2 hours as we did the check ins. Is this normal? What can we do to help if interval check ins aren’t working?", "Baby trained with a paid course at 5 months; wakings rise to 3-4 a night near 7 months.")
add("NewParents-1wshay4", None, "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "price_signal", ["contact_naps", "price_value", "short_naps"], "Try to nurse in glider, waste of $180, only works 20% of the time and for nights.", "Venting list of everything tried to get a 3-month-old to nap.")
add("NewParents-1wshay4", None, "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "pain", ["short_naps", "maternal_exhaustion"], "When baby finally goes to sleep only takes a fucking 30 minute nap. 45-1 hour if I’m lucky.", "After up to 1.5 hours of rocking and bouncing in the heat.")
add("NewParents-1wshay4", None, "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "others_said", ["conflicting_advice", "maternal_exhaustion"], "Everybody just scoffs at my struggle and says that I’m making it more complicated than it needs to be. I need to ENJOY it and it “goes by so fast blah blah blah”.", "Nearby family offers no help; husband had no paternity leave.")
add("NewParents-1wshay4", None, "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "pain", ["comparison_other_babies", "short_naps"], "It seems like everyone has all the answers and everyone else is just able to put their baby in a carrier or wrap in a blanket and walk around house or outside and baby magically goes to sleep.", "Mother feels like a failure next to other parents whose babies nap easily.")
add("NewParents-1wshay4", "pcmsbm3", "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "trigger_moment", ["regression_4_month", "feeding_to_sleep"], "Then 3 months hit and I was put in my place 😭 but thank you I’m looking forward to sleep training. Going to try a gentle Ferber", "Easy newborn who nursed to sleep for every nap changed at 3 months.")
add("sleeptrain-1wsi77i", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["partner_disagreement", "cry_it_out", "ferber"], "My husband is open to a full on CIO method, but that’s difficult for me so we’ve been doing a ferber-like method with some check-ins", "Started training at 6 months after reading a sleep book; baby had been waking about eight times a night.")
add("sleeptrain-1wsi77i", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["night_weaning", "feeding_to_sleep", "guilt"], "But I give in easily to BF him because I worry that he’s truly hungry.", "Mother struggles to hold the night-feed plan during sleep training.")
add("sleeptrain-1wsi77i", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "tried_failed", ["book_purchase", "cosleeping", "night_wakings"], "After reading Precious Little Sleep, we started sleep training our **6 month old** two nights ago. Prior to this, he was co-sleeping with us and had most recently been waking an average of 8 times a night", "A book, not a paid plan, started their sleep training.")
add("sleeptrain-1wsr744", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_24_36_months", "purchase", ["course_purchase", "sleep_consultant", "price_value"], "We added on a sleep consult to our sleep training course purchase with TCB and it was really helpful", "A course bought for the baby years earlier; a paid add-on consult helped when the 2-year-old became afraid of the crib.")
add("sleeptrain-1wsr744", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_24_36_months", "success_story", ["course_purchase"], "has been sleeping through the night since she was 8.5 months old and taking good naps. We did the Taking Cara Babies method and it worked wonders for her (and us!).", "Long-term course success described before a toddler setback.")
add("sleeptrain-1wt80q0", "pgq0u6e", "parent_unspecified", "looking_back", "failure_story", ["sleep_consultant", "wake_windows", "personalization"], "Even she was stumped as to why he wasn't sleeping better despite sleep training, she kept telling me to keep him awake longer and longer.", "Looking back at hiring a consultant at 5 months; the plan kept stretching wake windows.")
add("sleeptrain-1wt80q0", "pgq0u6e", "parent_unspecified", "looking_back", "pain", ["night_wakings", "sleep_consultant"], "He woke up every 30-60 minutes (and an average of 13 times per night) so he was exhausted for months.", "During the first consultant's plan.")
add("sleeptrain-1wt80q0", "pgq0u6e", "parent_unspecified", "looking_back", "success_story", ["sleep_consultant", "personalization"], "I hired a different sleep consultant right away who listened to me about his tendencies and by the end of the week he was sleeping through the night.", "Second consultant succeeded after the parent ignored wake windows for a day; the difference was being listened to.")
add("sleeptrain-1wt80q0", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "pain", ["night_wakings", "maternal_exhaustion"], "Between the newborn and him, I am up pretty much the entire night and getting 3 hours of broken sleep per night.", "Toddler nearly 2 waking nightly since a sibling arrived four weeks ago.")
add("sleeptrain-1wt80q0", "pet3wkx", "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "pain", ["night_wakings", "resentment"], "Worst part is my newborn has started sleeping 6 hour stretches, and I can't even take advantage of it because my toddler keeps me up for 2 hours every night.", "Schedule fix worked for five nights, then wakings returned.")
add("beyondthebumpUK-1wuervk", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_2_4_months", "purchase", ["app_tracking", "price_value"], "I’m just trialing Huckleberry, got the premium subscription on a 7 day trial and so far finding it quite good.", "Parent of an 11-week-old asks whether any baby apps are worth paying for.")
add("sleeptrain-1wullyg", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["sleep_consultant", "personalization", "wake_windows"], "Hired a sleep consultant and started sleep training the minute he hit 4 months. It also went like shit. 2.5 weeks of no improvement. Kept telling the consultant I thought he needed more wake time but she disagreed.", "Parents ended the consultant arrangement; at 6 months they are rocking, transferring and lost on schedule.")
add("sleeptrain-1wullyg", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "question", ["wake_windows", "information_overload"], "First baby so idk what I am doing. Would like to attempt sleep training again but lost on schedule.", "After a failed consultant plan, parent wants to retry alone.")
add("sleeptrain-1wuq7nl", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "objection", ["sleep_consultant", "feeding_to_sleep", "personalization"], "The consultant is insisting I keep waking him up to ensure he goes down awake in his cot, but this is really hard for a 15 minute feed and 20 minutes holding him upright for gas/reflux.", "Night two of consultant-supported modified Ferber with a breastfed baby; crying already halved.")
add("sleeptrain-1wv0c78", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "tried_failed", ["sleep_consultant", "short_naps"], "For naps she would sometimes cry 60 min without sleeping, so our former consultant changed the approach.", "Ten days into training an 8-month-old; parents now take wake-window advice from Reddit.")
add("sleeptrain-1wv0c78", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "trigger_moment", ["app_tracking", "early_waking"], "Bedtime: crib 9:35 PM → asleep 9:39 PM (4 min, completely on her own 🤯)", "Minute-by-minute log posted to strangers after one 5:45 AM waking.")
add("sleeptrain-1wvjwsz", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "pain", ["sleep_consultant", "guilt", "cry_it_out"], "I miss seeing my happy baby in the morning, when I walk in to wake her she starts crying now..", "Day 7 of controlled crying with a consultant funded by a condition charity's sleep scholarship.")
add("sleeptrain-1wvq8xs", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "objection", ["sleep_consultant", "regression_4_month", "schedule_rigidity"], "Our sleep coach recommends we train naps concurrently but that’s tough on our schedule right now, and we’re not in a rush for daytime crib naps to be a thing as we love our pram walks.", "Night training going well after 12 wake-ups a night in the 4-month regression.")
